    "created_at": "2017-03-01T14:02:29Z",
    "updated_at": "2017-03-01T14:02:29Z",
    "body": "What exactly would be the point of such flag on the request? Meaning, why not just allow to add headers or any potentially same-origin request (incl. `no-cors` and `navigate`), and just drop them when it goes to another origin?",
